 was also named head of  Walt Disney Animation Studios in 2018 on  the music front songwriters Kristen  anderson-lopez and Robert Lopez are  returning with 11 original new songs for  the soundtrack and Christophe Beck is  coming back to  pose the score the only significant  difference in the creative team between  frozen and frozen - is the screenwriters  while the original movie script was  penned by co-director Jennifer Lee  she'll share rating duties on the second  film with Alison Schroeder who wrote the  screenplay for 2018 s heartwarming  Christopher Robin Schroder was also  nominated for an Oscar for her  screenplay for 2017 s hidden figures  making her a strong addition to the  frozen teen frozen tells the tale of the  two daughters of the king and queen of  arendelle Elsa the elder sister and Anna  the younger one although the two were  closest children they drifted apart  after their parents taught Elsa that the  best way to deal with her magical icy  powers was to conceal them from the  world and to repress her emotions as a  result Elsa has isolated herself and  only poles further away when the king  and queen are lost at sea however as the  oldest daughter its  Elsa's duty to take up the crown but on  the day of her coronation she loses  control of her powers and flees the  kingdom onit pursues her into the  mountains aided by the ice Harvester  Kristoff and his trusty reindeer Sven  hoping to convince Elsa to end the  sudden winter she's created in Arundale  convinced she can't control her powers  Elsa accidentally freezes on his heart a  spell that will slowly kill her dying  and heartbroken honor returns to  Erindale where the sinister Hans is in  the midst of maneuvering to take control  of the kingdom but before he can kill  Elsa and seize the crown honest stops  him and her act of true love and saving  her sister thaws her heart  realizing love is the key to controlling  her powers Elsa ends the magical winter  reconciles with Anna and takes up her  crown as queen of arendelle  although six years will have passed for  us between frozen and frozen  - according to Disney's head of  animation Becky Brizzy the story of  frozen - will begin three years after  the end of the first film  Brizzy told The Hollywood Reporter it's  an evolution and an expansion of the  story of frozen and many of the  questions raised in the first movie  become the mystery  our gang are trying to solve in this  film she added that the main question of  frozen to will be why was Elsa born with  her powers your power will only grow  there is beauty in it  but also great danger but for anyone  worried that frozen to s mystery  centered storyline will be a departure  from the first film's focus on the  relationship between two sisters  you can put your fears to rest Disney's  head of effects Marlon West a short thr  that the sequel is ultimately quote  about two sisters trying to stay  together while the world tries to tear  them apart that sounds like exactly what  we'd hoped for after the emotional  family driven tale of the first film  based on the trailers Disney has  released four frozen two we can start to  piece together some of the plot in the  beginning all appears to be well in  Arundale with Queen also ruling  peacefully over her subjects from her  gently iced frosted castle but some sort  of malevolent unseen force manifesting  as pink flames drives the errand aliens  out of their homes determined to get to  the bottom of what's happened to them  and fix it  anna and elsa set off on a quest  accompanied by Kristoff Sven and Olaf  while the first film focused mostly on  Anna Elsa looks to be the main  protagonist of frozen - as she attempts  to track down the source of a mysterious  voice she hears calling to her she hopes  to discover the source of her powers and  through that knowledge somehow save her  kingdom  the trailers also indicate that an  enchanted forest in the far north will  prove to be significant to the two  sisters and possibly provides some  further clues about the backstory of  their parents in discussing the story  for frozen two directors Chris buck and  Jennifer Lee together with songwriters  Kristen anderson-lopez and Robert Lopez  realized they still had a few big  lingering questions after the events of  the first film  so they set about creating a story that  would answer them if the biggest  question is indeed why does Elsa have  her powers then that leads to a logical  follow-up  why doesn't Anna have powers in digging  into answers about the two sisters it  becomes obvious that we really need to  know more about their parents which  calls into question the circumstances  surrounding their deaths according to  Lee although the first film implied that  the king and queen were headed away on  roots  business when their ship sank things may  not all be as they appear during the  2019 d23 Expo Li T's the question where  were their parents really going when  that ship went down we've been promised  that the answers to all these questions  and more will be revealed in frozen -  although audiences were introduced  briefly to King Agner and Queen I Doudna  at the beginning of frozen they died  very early on in the film's narrative  and we learned almost nothing about them  at least nothing beyond their  instructions to Elsa concede don't fear  it ignore and die Doudna weren't given  names in the first film and had hardly  any lines for they're all too short  presents the Queen was voiced by  co-director Jennifer Lee with veteran  voice actor Maurice LaMarche  as the king for their expanded roles in  frozen 2 however the royal couple will  be voiced by Alfred Molina and Evan  Rachel Wood judging by her two songs on  the movie soundtrack I do know we'll  have a particularly hefty role and  according to Disney's press release the  Queen will begin to wonder if the  answers she seeks can be found in her  own past the press release has less to  say about Agner saying only that he'll  do anything to protect his daughters  from harm but the casting of the Golden  Globe and Emmy nominated Molina makes it  seem as though the king will have a  significant part to play as well  joining the impressive cast for frozen -  which includes nearly every major player  and a few returning minor characters  from the first movie is this is us  actors sterling K Brown who will be  voicing lieutenant Destin Mattias in  arendale soldier who's been trapped in  the enchanted forest for more than 30  years  lieutenant Mattias has according to  Disney's press release never forgotten  his sworn duty to Erindale but the  arrival of Queen Elsa and discovery that  she has magical powers is just the first  of many challenges to his long-held  beliefs  lieutenant Mattias originally travelled  to the forest to fight against the  nomadic north all drew people presumably  the enemies of Arundale however when we  see him in the trailer he and his men  appear to be standing alongside the  north ultra raising the question of  whether the animosity between the two  groups was some sort of MIS  standing or whether the trailer is  simply working to mislead us a  significant theme running through the  first frozen was about first impressions  being unreliable as evidenced with both  Elsa and Hans and we wouldn't be  surprised if it carries through to the  sequel in an even more prominent way  frozen may have had a compelling plot  but the sequel will be broadening the  scope of the series storytelling quite a  bit not only will Anna and Elsa be  venturing far outside the borders of  arendelle but they'll also be meeting  new people who at least at first glance  appear very different from them joining  the cast of frozen 2 are several members  of the north all drew people including  their leader Jelena the bold and brave  honey Maren and the eager fun-loving  Rider  according to Disney's press release  Alana is fiercely protective of her  family and community but is known to 